            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BRO01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William Cullen</forename>
                        <surname>Brown</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>surgeon</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Brown was the son of John Brown (1735-1788; <title>DNB</title>) who edited and published some of his
    father's works, but who seems to have been based in London for a period. A letter from him to Godwin shows Brown waiting to take the examination in surgery 
    and mentions the possibility of a placement in the Navy.</p>
                        <p> Brown's brothers include Ford Brown, who also appears in the diary (25 June 1812), and who was father of the painter Ford Maddox Brown.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 10, fols. 2-3: 1 September 1806</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">John Watkins, <title>A Biographical Dictionary of the Living Authors of Great Britain and Ireland</title> (London, 1816)</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
